---
import ServiceDetailLayout from '../../components/ServiceDetailLayout.astro';
import WorkbenchIcon from '../../components/WorkbenchIcon.astro';
import { serviceDetails } from '../../data/services';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import ServicePlatformMarks from '../../components/ServicePlatformMarks.astro';
import automationClay from '../../assets/concept-decorations/service-automation-clay.png';

const service = serviceDetails.automation;
const alternates = { en: 'https://haikaitech.my/services/automation/', bm: 'https://haikaitech.my/bm/services/automation/' };
---

<ServiceDetailLayout service={service} canonical={alternates.en} alternates={alternates}>
  <div slot="visual" class="sd-art sd-automation-art">
    <Image class="sd-clay-assembly sd-clay-assembly--automation" src={automationClay} alt="" width={1200} widths={[480, 800, 1200]} sizes="(max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 48px), (max-width: 1199px) 55vw, 720px" format="webp" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" />
    <ServicePlatformMarks kind="automation" />
  </div>

  <section slot="content" class="sd-content-section" aria-labelledby="automation-fit-title">
    <header class="sd-section-heading">
      <WorkbenchIcon name="workflow" size={22} />
      <h2 id="automation-fit-title">Start with the repeated bit.</h2>
      <p>Automation is most useful when it removes a clear handoff or keeps context moving between the tools your team already uses.</p>
    </header>
    <dl class="sd-row-list">
      <div class="sd-row"><dt>Enquiry intake</dt><dd>Capture an incoming request, sort the useful details and prepare the next human reply.</dd></div>
      <div class="sd-row"><dt>Team handoffs</dt><dd>Move information from one step to the next without making people copy the same context into every system.</dd></div>
      <div class="sd-row"><dt>Routine checks</dt><dd>Run a repeatable check or notification on a schedule, with a visible place for someone to review the result.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section slot="content" class="sd-content-section" aria-labelledby="automation-stack-title">
    <header class="sd-section-heading">
      <WorkbenchIcon name="settings" size={22} />
      <h2 id="automation-stack-title">The workshop has three tools.</h2>
      <p>Choose the smallest useful layer for the job. The technology follows the workflow, not the other way around.</p>
    </header>
    <dl class="sd-row-list">
      <div class="sd-row"><dt>Hermes agents</dt><dd>Set up an agent to work through a bounded task, with explicit instructions and a human checkpoint where needed.</dd></div>
      <div class="sd-row"><dt>n8n workflows</dt><dd>Connect services and repeatable steps visually, so the handoff is easier to inspect and maintain.</dd></div>
      <div class="sd-row"><dt>Custom scripts</dt><dd>Handle the edge cases that do not belong in a connector, with a small script shaped around your actual process.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section slot="content" class="sd-content-section" aria-labelledby="automation-proof-title">
    <header class="sd-section-heading">
      <WorkbenchIcon name="database" size={22} />
      <h2 id="automation-proof-title">Keep the system understandable.</h2>
      <p>Every automation handoff should be explainable, reviewable and possible to change when the business changes.</p>
    </header>
    <dl class="sd-row-list">
      <div class="sd-row"><dt>01 / Map</dt><dd>Describe the current process, where context gets lost and what “done” looks like.</dd></div>
      <div class="sd-row"><dt>02 / Build</dt><dd>Set up the smallest useful workflow, agent or script and test it against real examples.</dd></div>
      <div class="sd-row"><dt>03 / Handover</dt><dd>Document the moving parts, the human decisions and the next safe change.</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <div class="sd-proof">
      <p><strong>Related demo:</strong> the MZE Worker System shows the kind of operations thinking that can sit behind a workflow. It is a demo, not a client outcome claim.</p>
      <a href="https://mzdemo.haikaitech.my/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open the workforce demo</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</ServiceDetailLayout>
